Convincing us to take out more credit cards and to borrow money to buy more stuff. I think to understand the answer to that question, it's important to think about who ultimately is behind the money that is being offered to you. And it takes kind of a bigger picture perspective to try to answer that question. Who ultimately is so anxious to lend to you? That's when we come back. Economist Amir Sufi argues that we have failed to appreciate the role of household debt in economic crisis. We tend to think that something as big as a recession can only be caused by a tectonic upheaval, like a major financial company going under.

